  "body": "Depends on #1229. This branch contains its Hogan progress history; this group claims the frame controls and source corrections below. It will be synchronized with dev after that dependency merges, then complete final-head validation before merge.\n\nGreen Tree's seven-bay eaves, Sauganash's end openings and the first Tremont's shuttered corner form could not be expressed by the frame-tavern controls. Add optional controls for these features, raised entries, an opaque arch, explicitly reconstructed TREMONT lettering and a roof flag with its own date and confidence grade. Preserve the existing positional API and default geometry. The three hotels use the shared controls; their comparisons still **differ**, and the original image cases remain open. Dimensions, hidden treatment, lettering, colour, chronology and flag pose retain their evidence limits.\n\nCorrect St Mary's Andreas engraving credit and uncertain steeple chronology, distinguish Beaubien's homestead from the Factory House without resolving the panorama identification, and credit the jail and hotel drawings to Trowbridge in Gale's verified 1902 publication. Preserve retrospective date limits and the separate UCR copy's rights cautions. Photos exposes the existing catalogue title and publication holder. Both Gifford catalogue entries now agree with the source record: undated, attributed project use approved by the owner, with original publication and copyright status unresolved. No public-domain finding is claimed for Gifford.\n\nPinned Blender 4.5.3 regenerated all 23 affected frame-family masters and their real web derivatives. No preview master or recipe hash was substituted. The final Tremont reproduces the viewed export. Of 20 other legacy masters, 19 are byte-identical; one differs only in 66 bytes of unused UVs on untextured trim, with all geometry, material and confidence streams identical. No particular internal Blender cause is claimed.\n\nTremont's third storey also redistributes ordinary-capacity weights across six inns. Re-running the population draw from those weights would retire 30 invented identities and move existing lodgers. Extend the existing preservation policy with an explicit carried allocation basis: native rebuilding retains all 22 households, 157 person identities and 52 seats, while publishing current capacities. Report 37 physical vacancies and 5 occupants above the ordinary estimate separately from the net balance of 32. Staffing is limited by both physical room and the remaining historical allowance; later occupancy consumes that allowance, and another reweighting cannot replenish it. Quota, dated availability, house identity and crowded-capacity refusals remain enforced. Dated evidence can replace this reconstruction.\n\nValidation recorded so far:\n\n- Original-code/untouched-record comparison preserves all 23 producer-selected original frame phases, all 40 positional/API defaults and their old geometry, material and confidence streams. Unselected Sauganash 1829 passes separately. Feature, flag-anchor, form-consumer and name-pool checks pass.\n- The complete 23-master bake passes its contracts. Focused published card/flag QA passed 12/12 mobile and desktop cases with actual visible credits, grades and GPU flag checks and zero page/network/server errors. This precedes the capacity follow-up and does not substitute for the final full smoke suite.\n- The first grouped strict preflight failed 6 of 1,056 checks. Repairs cover the real flag reader in the version fixture, step-isolation records, native rights ratchet, lodging-model rebuild and ticket mirror continuity. Offset chimneys are measured against the actual roof under every cap: all four clear the unchanged 18-inch minimum, all 441 legacy readings remain exact, and independently shortening one stack fails. Model geometry is unchanged by this measurement repair.\n- Actual native lodging/staffing builds, checks and regression tests pass, including identity/seat preservation, fixed point, changed dates/crowding/class refusals, opposing vacancy/overflow and sequential allowance consumption. The incorrect aggregate-vacancy assertion is replaced with a counterexample; quota/crowded assertions remain intact. The reconstruction order book stays byte-exact. [Closed capacity evidence](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-tickets/blob/f9d23900b84567a156b631aab208774a04655591/evidence/image-match-2026-10-22/capacity-policy-history-20261023T134513Z/RECOVERY.md).\n\nCurrent checkpoint `792598d88056dbc768bb5062258a803c6a62524b` passes the corrected complete gate: **1,056 steps, none red**. The 55-step native refresh reaches a fixed point; the source tree is unchanged through the gate and equals the committed tree. Changelog and ticket-ID checks pass again on the actual new commit. Current-dev synchronization after #1229 and final published smoke coverage remain pending. This PR group completes shared generator capability and source corrections; it does not accept any original building image match.\n",
